# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-15, board 0.9); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: a laptop beside a larger monitor. Somebody has Notes lying across the two, low down, so that its left part also reaches
# below the laptop's lower edge: two fifths of it on the laptop, nearly half on the monitor, 85 % in view. They start Arbor.
# Nothing is docked, so nothing moves. Arbor used to ask each display by itself whether it showed half of the window, heard
# no twice, took it for lost and brought it to the middle of the laptop's display: at the start, and again at Quit.
# They dock it, think better of it, and Float All takes it back exactly where it was.
# Reference: "nothing moves until the person docks something"; collab/QUESTIONS.md, "two questions, two measures".
quiet
displays 2
relaunch quit
open Notes 800x600 at 1000 460
relaunch start
expect ok
expect still
expect at 101 1000 460
expect floating 101
wait 5
expect still

# Another window opens the same way, a little higher.
open Calendar 800x600 at 1010 440
expect still
expect at 102 1010 440
wait 5
expect still

# The keys that show everything have nothing to fetch.
press home
expect still
press show-all
expect still

# Docked, and given back.
dock 101 left
expect docked 101
float-all
expect at 101 1000 460
expect size 101 800x600
expect at 102 1010 440

# In the evening they quit Arbor, and in the morning it finds them there again.
relaunch quit
expect still
relaunch start
expect still
expect at 101 1000 460
expect at 102 1010 440
